    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198-a2">

                <pb facs="0374" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg312"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 17.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoppin to Mr. Clifton</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-09-16"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 16,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On my return on Saturday evening from
                    Liverpool, I found your note of the 13th, to which I could not conveniently
                    reply until this morning. I regret that you had not addressed it to the legation
                    (Members’ Buildings, Victoria street, corner of Great Chapel street), as I had
                    left instructions with Mr. Nadal, the second secretary, to send the money for
                    Condon, in case it should be required. However, I presume it will still reach
                    you in time for his purpose. I accordingly inclose my check to your order on the
                    London Westminster Bank for fifteen pounds, which please send to Condon on
                    behalf of Mr. Welsh, and also kindly acknowledge the receipt of this.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item>W. J. HOPPIN,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad
                                    interim</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">George Clifton</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Governor, Portland Prison, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                                    &amp;c</hi>.</item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
